---The App Runner resource that specifies an App Runner endpoint for incoming traffic. It establishes a connection between a VPC interface endpoint and a App Runner service, to make your App Runner service accessible from only within an Amazon VPC.
---@class aws.apprunner.VpcIngressConnection
---@field VpcIngressConnectionArn? aws.apprunner.AppRunnerResourceArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the VPC Ingress Connection.
---@field VpcIngressConnectionName? aws.apprunner.VpcIngressConnectionName The customer-provided VPC Ingress Connection name.
---@field ServiceArn? aws.apprunner.AppRunnerResourceArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the service associated with the VPC Ingress Connection.
---@field Status? aws.apprunner.VpcIngressConnectionStatus The current status of the VPC Ingress Connection. The VPC Ingress Connection displays one of the following statuses: AVAILABLE, PENDING_CREATION, PENDING_UPDATE, PENDING_DELETION,FAILED_CREATION, FAILED_UPDATE, FAILED_DELETION, and DELETED..
---@field AccountId? aws.apprunner.CustomerAccountId The Account Id you use to create the VPC Ingress Connection resource.
---@field DomainName? aws.apprunner.DomainName The domain name associated with the VPC Ingress Connection resource.
---@field IngressVpcConfiguration? aws.apprunner.IngressVpcConfiguration Specifications for the customer’s VPC and related PrivateLink VPC endpoint that are used to associate with the VPC Ingress Connection resource.
---@field CreatedAt? aws.apprunner.Timestamp The time when the VPC Ingress Connection was created. It's in the Unix time stamp format.
---@field DeletedAt? aws.apprunner.Timestamp The time when the App Runner service was deleted. It's in the Unix time stamp format.

---@alias aws.apprunner.VpcIngressConnectionName string

---@alias aws.apprunner.VpcIngressConnectionStatus "AVAILABLE"|"PENDING_CREATION"|"PENDING_UPDATE"|"PENDING_DELETION"|"FAILED_CREATION"|"FAILED_UPDATE"|"FAILED_DELETION"|"DELETED"

